From fe9831bcb4f2a614b790ae374a11a2bb170b1992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:26:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [Anti Detection] Make TEE Soft Generate mode
 fully software-owned

Treat Generate as a complete software TEE persona instead of allowing
its attestation path to depend on RKP availability.

Bypass RKP when no explicit attestation key is supplied. Continue to
load explicit ATTEST_KEY descriptors so their provenance can be
validated, but only accept keys owned by the software TEE persona.
Reject RKP and hardware-backed ATTEST_KEYs with INVALID_ARGUMENT and
never fall back to hardware generation when the software path fails.

Separate the public KeyEntry security-level UUID from the KeyMint UUID
that owns the blob. Keep generated keys attached to the genuine TEE
proxy while recording the SOFTWARE UUID only in blob metadata for
internal operation and ATTEST_KEY routing.

Recover keys written by the previous single-UUID implementation through
an on-demand cached software proxy, while continuing to report them as
TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT. This keeps persistent ATTEST_KEYs usable across
reboots without exposing the internal SOFTWARE backend.

Change-Id: I949b023510493c9c5d1c015d807e142ce980fd9a
---
 keystore2/src/security_level.rs | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 keystore2/src/service.rs        | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 keystore2/src/tee_soft_debug.rs | 14 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

